# Content and language

Each item is one JSON object: stable string `id`, bilingual `title`, image filename, verse arrays per language (`doha`, `chopai`), optional audio filename.

```json
{
  "id": "1",
  "title": { "hindi": "॥ श्री गणेश चालीसा ॥", "english": "Shri Ganesh Chalisa" },
  "image": "shriGanesh.webp",
  "audioUrl": "ganesh_chalisa.mp3"
}
```

- JSON stores filenames only. Register every image and audio file in a `require()` map (`chalisaMedia`). Resolve with `getDeityImageSource` and `getChalisaAudioSource`.
- Hide play controls when `hasChalisaAudio` is false. Next and previous skip items with no audio.
- UI copy lives in `translations.js` under `hindi` and `english`. Screens use `translations[language]`. Default language is `hindi`.
- Localized fields: `typeof value === 'object' ? value[language] : value`, then fall back to hindi, then english.

```javascript
// ❌ BAD
<Text>Favorites</Text>
<FastImage source={{ uri: item.image }} />

// ✅ GOOD
<Text>{t.favorites}</Text>
<FastImage source={getDeityImageSource(item.image)} />
```
